#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Tests for the two-stage content-verify layer
(content_verify.py, built 2026-11-17 per user decision 21:52
"Opsi A").

Proves, WITHOUT any real network (a deterministic FakeFetcher is
injected everywhere) and WITHOUT any real model call (a stub
model_call is injected) and WITHOUT launching any serve:

- TOKENS: percent / decimal / grouped / currency / full date /
  spelled-out percent are STRONG; bare years and bare integers
  are WEAK; identifier spans (RFC 5233, BIP-32, ePrint) never
  become tokens; figures inside a cited URL never become claim
  tokens (pointer spans are masked).
- PRESENCE: a percent token requires percent context in the
  source (a bare "50" proves nothing); grouped digits match with
  or without separators; dates match MDY/DMY/ISO forms; a
  spelled-out percent in the source matches a digit claim.
- CLAIMS: sentence pairing, paragraph fallback, repetition
  dedupe (the Hop closing repetition merges into the body claim),
  Sources-section lines generate no claims, unbound precision
  claims are recorded (not fatal).
- STAGE 1: the Hop pattern (live source, figures absent) is a
  pivotal finding and FATAL in block mode, never in shadow; a
  source carrying the figures supports; a bot-walled source puts
  the claim in the UNVERIFIABLE class (no finding, no block); a
  dead source is "no-source" (the citation layer owns death).
- STAGE 2: an unsupported entailment verdict is fatal; a
  supported verdict WITH a verbatim-verifiable evidence quote
  rescues a stage-1 finding; a supported verdict WITHOUT a
  verifiable quote degrades to unclear and the stage-1 finding
  stands; the call budget is honoured and skips are recorded; a
  raising model lane leaves stage-1 verdicts standing and is
  reported in `error`.
- CHECKER-FAILURE DOCTRINE: canary down -> available=False,
  verdict "unverified", nothing blocked.
- GATE: gate_answer without the stage reports content_verify NOT
  performed and the clean fixture stays sendable; a blocking
  content verdict withholds; a clean verdict keeps sendable; a
  crashing callable never withholds; the arming helper follows
  DIALECTICA_CONTENT_CHECK; the layer default mode is "block".
"""
